                            <div class="entry-content"><h4>Human antiviral CD8+ T cells activated</h4><p>In laboratory tests with liver cancer cells, CancerVax observed activation of human antiviral CD8+ T cells. The ELISpot assay measured T-cell activation, not cancer-cell killing.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/single-news.php?id=52">Read press release <svg class="arrow" width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12 12 4M5.5 4H12v6.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="/webinar-august-6-2026"><span class="play" aria-hidden="true"></span> Watch video</a></div><details><summary>View figure</summary><div class="figures"><figure><a href="<?php echo $full_url; ?>assets/images/progress2/progress-aug2026-image1.png" class="figure-link" aria-label="Enlarge figure: ELISpot results comparing T-cell activation across four human immune-cell preparations"><img loading="lazy" src="<?php echo $full_url; ?>assets/images/progress2/progress-aug2026-image1.png" alt="ELISpot results comparing T-cell activation across four human immune-cell preparations"></a><figcaption>ELISpot assay using human liver cancer cells</figcaption></figure></div></details></div>
