                            <div class="entry-content"><h4>Lower Smart mRNA activity in healthy liver cells</h4><p>Laboratory tests found substantially lower activity for Smart mRNA candidates for pancreatic and liver cancers in healthy human liver cells.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/single-news.php?id=42">Read press release <svg class="arrow" width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12 12 4M5.5 4H12v6.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></div><details><summary>View figure</summary><div class="figures"><figure><a href="<?php echo $full_url; ?>assets/images/progress2/dev-progress-4.png" class="figure-link" aria-label="Enlarge figure: Figure comparing Smart mRNA activity in healthy liver cells"><img loading="lazy" src="<?php echo $full_url; ?>assets/images/progress2/dev-progress-4.png" alt="Figure comparing Smart mRNA activity in healthy liver cells"></a><figcaption>Smart mRNA activity in laboratory tests</figcaption></figure></div></details></div>
