                            <div class="entry-content"><h4>Cancer cells elicited an antiviral T-cell response</h4><p>In laboratory tests, cancer cells treated with CancerVax Smart mRNA activated antiviral T cells. The study measured activation rather than direct killing of cancer cells.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/single-news.php?id=38">Read press release <svg class="arrow" width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12 12 4M5.5 4H12v6.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="/update-video-august-5-2025"><span class="play" aria-hidden="true"></span> Watch video</a></div><details><summary>View figure</summary><div class="figures"><figure><a href="<?php echo $full_url; ?>assets/images/progress2/t-cells-stimulatory.png" class="figure-link" aria-label="Enlarge figure: Chart comparing antiviral T-cell activation across study conditions"><img loading="lazy" src="<?php echo $full_url; ?>assets/images/progress2/t-cells-stimulatory.png" alt="Chart comparing antiviral T-cell activation across study conditions"></a><figcaption>T-cell activation compared with positive and negative controls</figcaption></figure></div></details></div>
